<title>POLAND: Polish zloty fixed higher at 3.17 pct from parity.</title>
<headline>Polish zloty fixed higher at 3.17 pct from parity.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0310 to the dollar, up from Thursday's 3.0335 and at 1.7985 to the mark, up from 1.8025, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.17 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Thursday's 2.90 percent fix. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
